hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2873","###\n Narrated to us by Muhammad bin Al-Ala' and Harun bin Ishaq, who both said: Narrated to us by Abu Khalid, who narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu Az-Zubayr, from Abu Ma'bad, from Ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) set out from Muzdalifah. When he descended into the valley of Muhasir, he said: \O people"","" use pebbles for throwing (at the Jamarat).\"" And"""""
"2874","**\nNarrated to us Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya and Bishr ibn Mu'adh who said: Narrated to us Bishr—he is the son of al-Mufaddal—who said: Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman—he is the son of Harmalah—on the authority of Yahya ibn Hind, on the authority of Harmalah ibn Amr al-Aslami who said:\n\nI performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). When we stood at Arafat, I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) placing one of his fingers upon the other. So I said to my maternal uncle, \O uncle"","" what is he saying?\"" He replied"","" \""He is saying: 'Throw the pebbles like the pebbles used in the game of al-Khadif.'\""\""\n\nBishr ibn Mu'adh also said: Yahya ibn Hind narrated to me on the authority of Harmalah who said: I performed Hajj.\n\nAbu Bakr (ibn Abi Shaybah) said: The maternal uncle of Harmalah ibn Amr is Sinan ibn Sannah"","" and Wahhab named him."""""
"2875","Narrated to us Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb with a rare narration: Narrated to us Abdur-Rahman bin Sulayman, on the authority of Ubaydullah, on the authority of Abu Az-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir (RA), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) threw the pebbles at the Jamrah with stones the size of those used for slinging.\"""""""
